  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ABG - Realising the Faith Potential</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project entails several activities that include, training, visits, advocacy within regional economic groupings, strengthening the parliamentary liaison desks and cross-learning experience between IMBISA, ACEAC and AMECEA. . This project aims at sensitizing Church leaders on their prophetic through the already established structures like Justice and Peace, PLOs and so on. We will hold a meeting of the national commissions, PLO officers to keep track of the implementation efforts of the Synod on governance and strategizing together on the same. In this we intend to key in the Synod propositions regarding governance in the way the Church will continue doing advocacy for transparency. The projects targets at having the Church advocate for policies that will discourage corruption and promote transparency. We will produce an advocacy tool in form of a documentary that will show the levels of poverty in Kenya and Uganda as sampled country, and how this is linked to corruption and bad governance. This aims at creating awareness within the Church and the general public on the importance of accountability in governance. This will come as an appeal to every individual to practice honesty and condemn dishonesty at all levels. It is also meant to trigger more enthusiasm of all stake-holders working for good governance. It is meant to create a link between governance and the situation of the people, hence making governance a concern of the people.The training of trainers (TOT) workshops on advocacy, targeting commissioners of CJPCs pertinent Catholic Bishop/s and leaders of other churches has been on course.  This will be done through seeking accreditation in such meetings or parallel activities that would make the stand of the Church clear. In order to enrich and harmonize our efforts within our jurisdiction, AMECEA will organize a cross-learning meeting between IMBISA, AMECEA and ACEAC.</narrative>
  </description>
